  "body": "Add 2D abrasive-waterjet verification laws and connect them to the posting gate (`crates/sim` and `crates/app`).\n\nDepends on #1883 (`WaterjetProfile`).\n\n## Scope\n\n- **2D through-cut verifier (`crates/sim/src/verify/`):**\n  - Share crossing, order, kerf-band gouge, and tip-up helpers with `crates/sim/src/verify/plasma/` while supporting open chains from tab gaps.\n  - Check cut order: warn or refuse when an inner contour runs after an untabbed enclosing outer contour.\n  - Check kerf crossing: warn when a lit path crosses or enters within one kerf width of an earlier kerf or void.\n  - Check tip-up hazard: warn when a jet-off rapid crosses a freed, untabbed cutout region, and clear valid tabbed contours cleanly.\n  - Check 2D gouge: refuse when any kerf-offset band cuts into the target part boundary beyond tolerance.\n  - Check bed travel envelope: verify every move and arc bulge sits inside stated XY bed travel, including asymmetric bounds like `X 0..460` and `Y -305..0` mm.\n- **Post gate (`crates/app/src/posting*.rs`, `crates/app/src/machine/`):**\n  - Run waterjet 2D laws instead of 3D dexel stock simulation, and note the skipped 3D stock sim like `posting_plasma.rs`.\n  - Block posting on any blocking finding per Prime Directive.\n\n**Done means:** every waterjet law has passing and failing test fixtures (including tabbed vs untabbed cutouts), tests verify asymmetric bed bounds checks, and blocking findings stop posting at the program gate.\n\nPart of #1525\n",
